---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>

  <!-- Nav -->
  <header class="border-b border-slate-800">
    <nav class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 h-16 flex items-center justify-between">
      <span class="text-white font-semibold tracking-tight text-lg">MeshWhisper</span>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 text-sm text-slate-400">
        <a href="https://relay.meshwhisper.org/health" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Status</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/antonmannering/meshwhisper" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">GitHub</a>
        <a href="#get-started" class="bg-brand-500 hover:bg-brand-400 text-white px-4 py-1.5 rounded-md font-medium transition-colors">Get started</a>
      </div>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pt-24 pb-20 text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-brand-950/60 border border-brand-800/50 text-brand-300 text-xs font-medium px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full mb-8">
        <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand-400"></span>
        Post-quantum secure · X3DH + ML-KEM-768 + Double Ratchet
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-5xl sm:text-6xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight leading-tight mb-6">
        Encrypted messaging<br />your app <em class="not-italic text-brand-400">cannot read</em>
      </h1>

      <p class="text-xl text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-10 leading-relaxed">
        Add end-to-end encrypted messaging to any app — PWA, React Native, or Node.js —
        with a few lines of code and one Docker container you run yourself.
        Messages are encrypted on the device. Your server forwards opaque ciphertext. That's all it can do.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a href="#get-started" class="bg-brand-500 hover:bg-brand-400 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold transition-colors">
          Get started
        </a>
        <a href="https://relay.meshwhisper.org/health" class="border border-slate-700 hover:border-slate-500 text-slate-300 hover:text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold transition-colors">
          Live relay ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Comparison callout -->
    <section class="border-y border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-8 text-center">
        <div>
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-1">~€4<span class="text-slate-500 text-lg font-normal">/mo</span></div>
          <div class="text-slate-400 text-sm">Your VPS. Not our servers.</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-1">3 lines</div>
          <div class="text-slate-400 text-sm">To add messaging to your app</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-1">0 messages</div>
          <div class="text-slate-400 text-sm">We can read. Structurally impossible.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it works -->
    <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-24">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white text-center mb-4">How it works</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-center max-w-xl mx-auto mb-16">
        The protocol is Signal-grade end-to-end encryption. Your node is a dumb forwarder — it moves encrypted blobs and nothing more.
      </p>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
        <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-900 border border-brand-700 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-300 font-bold mb-4">1</div>
          <h3 class="text-white font-semibold mb-2">Install the SDK</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Add <code class="text-brand-300 bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">@meshwhisper/sdk</code> to your app.
            Call <code class="text-brand-300 bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">MeshWhisper.init()</code>.
            The SDK handles key generation, X3DH handshakes, and the Double Ratchet automatically.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-900 border border-brand-700 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-300 font-bold mb-4">2</div>
          <h3 class="text-white font-semibold mb-2">Run your node</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            One Docker container on a €4/month VPS. It routes encrypted packets, queues messages for offline users,
            and wakes devices via push notifications. It cannot decrypt anything.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-900 border border-brand-700 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-300 font-bold mb-4">3</div>
          <h3 class="text-white font-semibold mb-2">Your users message</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Messages are encrypted on the sender's device and decrypted on the recipient's device.
            Your server — and ours — never see plaintext. Not by policy. By mathematics.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Architecture diagram -->
    <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pb-24">
      <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-8 font-mono text-sm">
        <div class="text-slate-500 mb-4 text-xs">// What the node sees</div>
        <div class="grid gap-3 text-slate-300">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
            <span class="text-brand-400 w-28 shrink-0">Alice's device</span>
            <span class="text-slate-600">→</span>
            <span class="text-slate-400">encrypt("Hello Bob")</span>
            <span class="text-slate-600">→</span>
            <span class="text-slate-500 italic">0x4f8a2c...</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
            <span class="text-yellow-400 w-28 shrink-0">Your node</span>
            <span class="text-slate-600">→</span>
            <span class="text-slate-400">forward(</span>
            <span class="text-slate-500 italic">0x4f8a2c...</span>
            <span class="text-slate-400">)</span>
            <span class="text-slate-600 ml-2">← that's all</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
            <span class="text-brand-400 w-28 shrink-0">Bob's device</span>
            <span class="text-slate-600">→</span>
            <span class="text-slate-400">decrypt(</span>
            <span class="text-slate-500 italic">0x4f8a2c...</span>
            <span class="text-slate-400">)</span>
            <span class="text-slate-600 mx-2">→</span>
            <span class="text-green-400">"Hello Bob"</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Why different -->
    <section class="border-t border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-24">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white text-center mb-4">Why not just use Sendbird?</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-center max-w-xl mx-auto mb-16">
          Hosted messaging services can read everything your users send. MeshWhisper cannot — and neither can you.
        </p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-slate-800">
                <th class="text-left text-slate-500 font-medium py-3 pr-8 w-40"></th>
                <th class="text-center text-white font-semibold py-3 px-4">MeshWhisper</th>
                <th class="text-center text-slate-400 font-medium py-3 px-4">Sendbird / Stream</th>
                <th class="text-center text-slate-400 font-medium py-3 px-4">Build yourself</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60">
              {[
                ['Monthly cost', '~€4 (your VPS)', '$2,000+', 'Engineers × months'],
                ['Can read messages', '✗ Impossible', '✓ Yes', 'Depends on you'],
                ['Time to integrate', '2–4 hours', '1–2 days', 'Months'],
                ['Push notifications', '✓ Included', 'Add-on', 'Build separately'],
                ['Message history', '✓ Included', '✓ Included', 'Build separately'],
                ['Post-quantum crypto', '✓ ML-KEM-768', '✗ No', 'Very hard'],
                ['You own the data', '✓ Always', '✗ Their servers', '✓ Always'],
              ].map(([feature, mw, sb, diy]) => (
                <tr>
                  <td class="py-3 pr-8 text-slate-400">{feature}</td>
                  <td class="py-3 px-4 text-center text-white font-medium">{mw}</td>
                  <td class="py-3 px-4 text-center text-slate-500">{sb}</td>
                  <td class="py-3 px-4 text-center text-slate-500">{diy}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Use cases -->
    <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-24">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white text-center mb-4">Who it's for</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-center max-w-xl mx-auto mb-16">
        Any app where your users' privacy matters and you want to prove it structurally, not just claim it in a privacy policy.
      </p>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
        {[
          {
            icon: '🏥',
            title: 'Healthcare',
            body: 'Patient–doctor messaging where you structurally cannot access patient communications. E2EE is your compliance argument.',
          },
          {
            icon: '⚖️',
            title: 'Legal',
            body: 'Lawyer–client communications where privilege requires confidentiality. No subpoena can produce what the server never stored.',
          },
          {
            icon: '💼',
            title: 'Finance',
            body: 'Advisor–client messaging under increasing regulatory pressure toward E2EE. Tell clients their data is safe — and prove it.',
          },
          {
            icon: '📱',
            title: 'Any app',
            body: 'Adding messaging to your product? Skip the six-month build and the privacy liability. Your users deserve E2EE by default.',
          },
        ].map(({ icon, title, body }) => (
          <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6">
            <div class="text-3xl mb-3">{icon}</div>
            <h3 class="text-white font-semibold mb-2">{title}</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">{body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Get started -->
    <section id="get-started" class="border-t border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-24">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white text-center mb-4">Get started</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-center mb-16">
          You can use the Foundation-hosted relay at <code class="text-brand-300">wss://relay.meshwhisper.org</code> for development.
          Run your own node in production.
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div>
            <div class="text-slate-500 text-xs font-medium mb-2 font-mono">1. Install</div>
            <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5 font-mono text-sm">
              <span class="text-slate-500">$</span> <span class="text-white">npm install @meshwhisper/sdk</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <div class="text-slate-500 text-xs font-medium mb-2 font-mono">2. Initialize</div>
            <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed">
              <span class="text-brand-400">import</span> <span class="text-white">{'{ MeshWhisper }'}</span> <span class="text-brand-400">from</span> <span class="text-green-400">'@meshwhisper/sdk'</span><span class="text-slate-300">;</span><br /><br />
              <span class="text-brand-400">const</span> <span class="text-white">mw</span> <span class="text-slate-400">=</span> <span class="text-brand-400">await</span> <span class="text-yellow-300">MeshWhisper</span><span class="text-slate-300">.</span><span class="text-blue-300">init</span><span class="text-slate-300">({'({'}</span><br />
              <span class="text-slate-300">&nbsp;&nbsp;namespace</span><span class="text-slate-400">:</span> <span class="text-green-400">'com.example.myapp'</span><span class="text-slate-300">,</span><br />
              <span class="text-slate-300">&nbsp;&nbsp;node</span><span class="text-slate-400">:</span> <span class="text-green-400">'wss://relay.meshwhisper.org'</span><span class="text-slate-300">,</span><br />
              <span class="text-slate-300">&nbsp;&nbsp;onMessage</span><span class="text-slate-400">:</span> <span class="text-slate-300">(msg)</span> <span class="text-brand-400">=&gt;</span> <span class="text-yellow-300">console</span><span class="text-slate-300">.</span><span class="text-blue-300">log</span><span class="text-slate-300">(msg),</span><br />
              <span class="text-slate-300">{'})'}</span><span class="text-slate-300">;</span><br /><br />
              <span class="text-slate-500">// X3DH key exchange happens automatically on first contact</span><br />
              <span class="text-brand-400">await</span> <span class="text-yellow-300">MeshWhisper</span><span class="text-slate-300">.</span><span class="text-blue-300">send</span><span class="text-slate-300">(contactId, payload);</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <div class="text-slate-500 text-xs font-medium mb-2 font-mono">3. Deploy your node (production)</div>
            <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed">
              <span class="text-slate-500">$</span> <span class="text-white">docker run -d \</span><br />
              <span class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;-p 8080:8080 \</span><br />
              <span class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;-v meshwhisper_data:/data \</span><br />
              <span class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;-e BASE_URL=https://relay.myapp.com \</span><br />
              <span class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;ghcr.io/meshwhisper/node:latest</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Security section -->
    <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-24">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white text-center mb-4">The cryptography</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-center max-w-xl mx-auto mb-16">
        Built on audited, peer-reviewed primitives. No homebrew crypto.
      </p>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        {[
          {
            title: 'Post-quantum key exchange (PQXDH)',
            body: 'Hybrid X3DH + ML-KEM-768. Sessions are secure against both classical and quantum adversaries from the first message. Matches Signal\'s PQXDH specification.',
          },
          {
            title: 'Double Ratchet',
            body: 'Every message uses a fresh key. Compromise of one key exposes neither past nor future messages. Implemented to the Signal specification with out-of-order delivery support.',
          },
          {
            title: 'Safety numbers',
            body: 'Signal-style 60-digit verification codes. Both parties compute the same number from their Ed25519 identity keys. Compare out-of-band to verify no MITM.',
          },
          {
            title: 'Audited primitives',
            body: '@noble/curves, @noble/ciphers, @noble/hashes, @noble/post-quantum. Pure JavaScript, no WASM, no native bindings. Runs identically in browser, Node.js, and React Native.',
          },
        ].map(({ title, body }) => (
          <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-white font-semibold mb-2">{title}</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">{body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer class="border-t border-slate-800">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-between gap-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
      <div>
        <div class="text-white font-semibold mb-1">MeshWhisper</div>
        <div>End-to-end encrypted messaging for any app.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-8">
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <div class="text-slate-400 font-medium">Developers</div>
          <div><a href="https://github.com/antonmannering/meshwhisper" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">GitHub</a></div>
          <div><a href="https://relay.meshwhisper.org/health" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Relay status</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <div class="text-slate-400 font-medium">Protocol</div>
          <div><a href="https://github.com/antonmannering/meshwhisper/blob/main/docs/whitepaper.md" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Whitepaper</a></div>
          <div><a href="https://github.com/antonmannering/meshwhisper/blob/main/docs/api.md" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">API reference</a></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>

</Layout>
